This source tree contains separately licensed parts.

Project runtime contributions and compatible replacement implementations use
GPL-2.0-or-later where marked. Original LGPL, MIT and BSD notices remain effective.

Original HDR10 AI, model-adapter, circuit and policy modules are now offered
under GPL-2.0-or-later by their owner. Replacement cache, metadata-bounds,
serializer and CM4 wire helpers use GPL-2.0-or-later. Retained third-party notices still apply.
Original HDR10+ serialization, analysis, curve fitting and DV metadata adapters
are included under the same project-owner GPL-2.0-or-later direction. They reuse
the current GPL-2.0-compatible creative implementation, not the former GPLv3
dependency implementations. Third-party code is not covered by this grant.
The replacement canonical tunnel shader, GL packer, vertex and generated-source
wrapper and replacement fused composition use GPL-2.0-or-later.

Original frame transactions, Master Reference contract, processing preparation,
GL frame adapter and CPU Adaptive model use GPL-2.0-or-later under the owner's
grant. This does not relicense their separately implemented dependencies.

The scalar creative module combines original CM4/resolver/fitter code with
replacement numerical kernels under GPL-2.0-or-later; see the migration record.

The original Adaptive shader and replacement GPU trim/carrier/composition kernels
use GPL-2.0-or-later. Original FEL, metadata-validation and player adapters receive
the owner's additional grant. Imported implementations are replaced separately,
not covered by that grant.

Original tooling/documentation is MIT where declared. The FFmpeg-derived filter
retains LGPL-2.1-or-later. Dependency patches include both inherited LGPL code and
compatible project additions; see docs/GPL2-MIGRATION.md. Upstream LibreELEC and
dependency declarations/build conditions are unchanged. Test-only oracles retain
their per-file licenses and are not linked into the runtime.

The exact L1/L3 model bundle is offered under GPL-2.0-or-later by its owner.
LightGBM itself is MIT. See models/l1l3/LICENSE.md.

